      "line_end": 20,
      "title": "Decimal multiplied by float raises TypeError",
      "description": "The total field holds a Decimal, and apply_discount multiplies it by the float 0.9. Python raises TypeError for Decimal times float. Every redeem request with the valid code fails with a server error. No user can ever apply the discount. Multiply by Decimal(\"0.9\") and quantize the result to two decimal places.",
      "suggested_change": "        self.total = (self.total * Decimal(\"0.9\")).quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"))",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
